    deepExplanation: "An external store is state managed outside React, such as a browser API, custom store, or third-party state library. React needs a subscription mechanism so components re-render when the store changes while maintaining consistent snapshots.\\n\\n```ts\ntype Listener = () => void;\n\nlet value = 0;\nconst listeners = new Set<Listener>();\n\nexport const store = {\n  getSnapshot: () => value,\n  subscribe(listener: Listener) {\n    listeners.add(listener);\n    return () => listeners.delete(listener);\n  },\n  increment() {\n    value++;\n    listeners.forEach(listener => listener());\n  },\n};\n```\\n\\nWhy it matters: This topic affects correctness, maintainability, responsiveness, or scalability in production React applications.",
